      "content": [],
      "prompt": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "For a certain circuit, its power p, in wats, current C, in amperes; voltage y, in volts; and resistance R, in ohms, are related as $\\frac{CV^2}{P}=\\sqrt{PR}$ ，where P, C, V, and R are positive. When R=18, which equation correctly expresses P in terms of C and V ?"
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "kind": "gengdu-export",
        "sourceSetId": "gengdu-offline-fcc8fa63d892489dabcdd693691dd7a6",
        "sourceQuestionId": "6081442",
        "url": "https://gengdu.shanmaostar.com"
      },
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "choice-a",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "$P=\\frac{CV^2}{\\sqrt{18P}}$"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "choice-b",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "$P=\\frac{CV^2}{\\sqrt{18}}$"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "choice-c",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "$P=\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{C^2V^4}{18}}$"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "choice-d",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "$P=\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{18}{C^2V^4}}$"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
