          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "$\\frac{49}{p}=\\frac{49}{q}-\\frac{49}{r}-\\frac{49}{s}$   \nThe given equation relates the positive variables p, q, r, and s. Which of the following is equivalent to q?"
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "kind": "gengdu-export",
        "sourceSetId": "gengdu-offline-fcc8fa63d892489dabcdd693691dd7a6",
        "sourceQuestionId": "6081443",
        "url": "https://gengdu.shanmaostar.com"
      },
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "choice-a",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "$p+r+s$"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "choice-b",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "$49\\left(p+r+s\\right)$"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "choice-c",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "$\\frac{prs}{pr+ps+rs}$"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "choice-d",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "$\\frac{prs}{49p+49r+49s}$"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
